1
00:00:19,330 --> 00:00:20,540
Who found the bodies?

2
00:00:21,130 --> 00:00:24,340
An officer found the first.
Currently there are two corpses.

3
00:00:24,370 --> 00:00:27,140
One missing his head.
The other corpse's forehead is carved.

4
00:00:27,225 --> 00:00:30,300
The first corpse is over there.
There's the evidence and the body.

5
00:00:30,850 --> 00:00:31,620
Thank you.

6
00:00:36,410 --> 00:00:38,940
The villagers heard loud screams.

7
00:00:39,050 --> 00:00:40,900
Followed by a sudden silence.

8
00:00:41,010 --> 00:00:42,260
They thought it was just a drunk.

9
00:00:43,010 --> 00:00:45,420
Pong, a friend of the deceased,
is the person who found him.

10
00:00:47,170 --> 00:00:48,500
A fisherman's corpse.

11
00:00:49,010 --> 00:00:50,740
His forehead carved with
Khmer alphabets.

12
00:00:51,450 --> 00:00:52,740
The other is headless.

13
00:00:54,010 --> 00:00:55,700
What the hell is happening in this town?

14
00:00:56,530 --> 00:00:58,020
The body that was carved...

15
00:00:58,210 --> 00:01:00,860
Is he possibly related to the suspect,
Mr. Bong Pra-on?

16
00:01:02,450 --> 00:01:03,780
Very likely.

17
00:01:08,090 --> 00:01:08,860
Sergeant Ming!

18
00:01:09,690 --> 00:01:10,460
Sergeant Ming!

19
00:01:11,090 --> 00:01:11,620
Yes?

20
00:01:13,410 --> 00:01:17,380
Tell everyone to secure the area
and find that head.

21
00:01:17,850 --> 00:01:20,260
- Look everywhere on the beach.
- Yes. I'm on it, sir.

22
00:01:22,210 --> 00:01:22,980
Yes, sir.

23
00:01:23,170 --> 00:01:24,460
Go, go check it out.

24
00:01:25,370 --> 00:01:26,220
Superintendent.

25
00:01:26,855 --> 00:01:29,500
We have no fingerprint
evidence from the killer.

26
00:01:29,530 --> 00:01:32,620
There are only some prints...
faint, fragmented, incomplete.

27
00:01:33,150 --> 00:01:34,460
It doesn't look like he wore gloves.

28
00:01:34,935 --> 00:01:36,700
It's as if the killer
has no fingerprints, sir.

29
00:01:40,970 --> 00:01:43,140
Besides this evidence,
is there anything else?

30
00:01:44,170 --> 00:01:44,780
Yes, sir.

31
00:01:46,545 --> 00:01:47,820
The spot we're standing on...

32
00:01:48,730 --> 00:01:50,860
It's the center of a Khmer ritual place.

33
00:03:08,330 --> 00:03:10,420
Who are you?
Where are you from? What's your name?

34
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:17,420
I don't know.

35
00:03:18,890 --> 00:03:19,980
Sounds like trouble.

36
00:03:20,130 --> 00:03:21,140
Alzheimer's?

37
00:03:24,930 --> 00:03:28,260
You walked from the sea
to the shore. We rescued you.

38
00:03:28,610 --> 00:03:29,420
Where are you from?

39
00:03:33,645 --> 00:03:35,220
Where's your home? Do you remember?

40
00:03:35,500 --> 00:03:36,260
So we can take you there.

41
00:03:42,930 --> 00:03:43,700
I don't know.

42
00:03:44,490 --> 00:03:47,700
Huh? What about your name? Your name?

43
00:03:48,050 --> 00:03:48,900
Do you remember?

44
00:03:56,010 --> 00:03:57,540
I don't know.

45
00:03:58,925 --> 00:03:59,940
Oh.

46
00:04:01,490 --> 00:04:02,660
Perfect.

47
00:04:02,930 --> 00:04:04,980
Patient care. That's your job now.

48
00:04:05,515 --> 00:04:06,460
Yeah, my job.

49
00:04:12,225 --> 00:04:14,260
Oh, hey! You're awake.

50
00:04:14,490 --> 00:04:15,060
Mm-hmm.

51
00:04:28,490 --> 00:04:31,140
Even in the jungle,
you can still find booze to drink.

52
00:04:34,890 --> 00:04:39,500
You don't know anything.
The forest foragers have their ways.

53
00:04:39,970 --> 00:04:43,060
There are hidden stashes
of the good stuff. They ferment it...

54
00:04:43,090 --> 00:04:45,100
and bury it in bamboo thickets.

55
00:04:45,450 --> 00:04:47,625
Whoever drinks it all,
makes a new batch.

56
00:04:47,930 --> 00:04:52,025
For the newcomers.
It's passed down through the generations.

57
00:04:53,050 --> 00:04:53,980
Guys like us...

58
00:04:54,890 --> 00:04:56,460
never go thirsty.

59
00:04:58,290 --> 00:05:00,580
When the Burmese come,
you'd better save your own skin.

60
00:05:01,315 --> 00:05:02,900
I won't save you for sure.

61
00:05:04,350 --> 00:05:05,440
Let them come.

62
00:05:07,690 --> 00:05:09,740
I'll chop them with my axe.

63
00:05:11,875 --> 00:05:15,140
You just reek of liquor.
The Burmese will smell you first.

64
00:05:15,970 --> 00:05:18,660
No wonder when we go to the village...

65
00:05:19,250 --> 00:05:21,460
the villagers call you "Stinky Thong."

66
00:05:22,230 --> 00:05:23,380
You really do stink.

67
00:05:28,755 --> 00:05:30,220
Hey, Man.

68
00:05:32,330 --> 00:05:33,740
Why are you tying charms again, brother?

69
00:05:34,530 --> 00:05:35,940
Has your spell weakened?

70
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:42,605
I remember there was one commander
our blades couldn't cut.

71
00:05:43,965 --> 00:05:45,540
He must have a strong discipline.

72
00:05:47,455 --> 00:05:49,300
And their numbers will keep growing.

73
00:05:50,495 --> 00:05:52,180
They're starting to realize we're here.

74
00:05:53,480 --> 00:05:55,380
They must observe, just like we do.

75
00:05:56,670 --> 00:05:58,140
Whenever there's a fight...

76
00:05:59,645 --> 00:06:01,940
they must report to their commanders.

77
00:06:04,550 --> 00:06:06,380
So what should we do, brother?

78
00:06:08,420 --> 00:06:10,340
They must have protective amulets.

79
00:06:15,815 --> 00:06:16,980
Take their charms away.

80
00:06:18,250 --> 00:06:19,380
Then kill them.

81
00:06:21,330 --> 00:06:22,660
Speaking of protective charms...

82
00:06:24,130 --> 00:06:25,380
Where has Khong gone?

83
00:06:26,010 --> 00:06:26,780
Yeah.

84
00:06:28,370 --> 00:06:31,740
Countering dark magic,
it's be Khong's expertise.

85
00:06:32,170 --> 00:06:34,020
The number one sorcerer.

86
00:06:34,890 --> 00:06:35,900
So tough.

87
00:06:36,250 --> 00:06:38,260
Lately, he's been acting strange, brother.

88
00:06:38,570 --> 00:06:41,140
Seems obsessed with talking about
summoning spirits or something.

89
00:06:43,520 --> 00:06:44,900
- Hey!
- Khong!

90
00:06:47,265 --> 00:06:47,820
Khong.

91
00:06:50,730 --> 00:06:52,020
Khong, where have you been?

92
00:06:53,205 --> 00:06:56,300
I went to catch a jungle fowl.
Ran into Burmese soldiers.

93
00:06:57,015 --> 00:06:59,420
So I killed them and left them
at the edge of the forest over there.

94
00:07:00,930 --> 00:07:03,380
They're... getting closer all the time.

95
00:07:06,195 --> 00:07:08,980
Khong... you're bleeding.

96
00:07:09,570 --> 00:07:10,780
You're bleeding a lot.

97
00:07:12,250 --> 00:07:13,020
Damn.

98
00:07:13,610 --> 00:07:14,900
Even someone like Khong got hit?

99
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:16,940
They must have powerful charms.

100
00:07:18,010 --> 00:07:18,780
Right.

101
00:07:19,610 --> 00:07:21,220
One of them is strong with magic.

102
00:07:22,090 --> 00:07:23,460
We must behead him.

103
00:07:25,335 --> 00:07:26,220
Huh?

104
00:07:26,640 --> 00:07:27,860
What about my Uncle In?

105
00:07:28,795 --> 00:07:29,500
Uh...

106
00:07:30,370 --> 00:07:32,940
In went to send a message to Ban Rajan.

107
00:07:33,610 --> 00:07:34,780
He'll be back tomorrow.

108
00:07:36,585 --> 00:07:38,460
In two watches' time.

109
00:07:39,335 --> 00:07:40,580
Those damn Burmese...

110
00:07:41,810 --> 00:07:44,060
Their army will surely march here.

111
00:08:12,315 --> 00:08:14,900
Yeah, quitting is good.
You should back off, man.

112
00:08:15,440 --> 00:08:16,740
It's a complete mess now.

113
00:08:17,475 --> 00:08:18,740
With those damn Russians...

114
00:08:18,970 --> 00:08:20,220
Koreans, Thais...

115
00:08:20,770 --> 00:08:22,060
It's a goddamn free-for-all.

116
00:08:22,610 --> 00:08:23,580
Yeah, damn it.

117
00:08:23,980 --> 00:08:27,420
And then, just like I thought,
that prick threatened me. He said...

118
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:29,540
"The boss will come down himself soon."

119
00:08:30,290 --> 00:08:31,900
Pff! Screw that bastard.

120
00:08:32,490 --> 00:08:34,460
Like we're scared of him, damn it!

121
00:08:34,810 --> 00:08:36,300
You just watch your own back, Tun.

122
00:08:37,050 --> 00:08:39,340
When the new shipment comes,
don't you take it. Understood?

123
00:08:39,890 --> 00:08:40,660
Yeah, yeah.

124
00:08:41,730 --> 00:08:43,660
That's it for now. The dealer is coming
for the booze payment.

125
00:08:52,090 --> 00:08:52,660
Singh!

126
00:08:53,795 --> 00:08:57,580
Kongdej told you to recite something, yes?
That note he gave you...

127
00:08:57,605 --> 00:08:58,580
Have you been doing it at all?

128
00:08:59,170 --> 00:08:59,900
Huh?

129
00:09:01,150 --> 00:09:02,100
No, Mom.

130
00:09:03,495 --> 00:09:04,780
Do you listen him at all?

131
00:09:08,640 --> 00:09:10,500
You never care about a thing.

132
00:09:11,130 --> 00:09:12,980
Teens these days only
listen to themselves.

133
00:09:14,410 --> 00:09:16,140
At least pray to the elders sometimes.

134
00:09:16,810 --> 00:09:19,590
He gave you a chant, so use it.
Good things might come your way.

135
00:09:20,090 --> 00:09:22,460
I'm talking so much my mouth
is about to split to my ears.

136
00:09:24,450 --> 00:09:25,460
Do you hear me?

137
00:10:02,625 --> 00:10:04,180
Memorize it by heart, Singh.

138
00:10:05,605 --> 00:10:06,620
Don't let anyone see it.

139
00:10:07,935 --> 00:10:09,340
Read it, then burn it.

140
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:20,660
Incantation to transform
tamarind leaves into hornets.

141
00:10:23,050 --> 00:10:24,260
Matyano

142
00:10:24,910 --> 00:10:26,210
Matya...

143
00:10:33,905 --> 00:10:35,460
Where am I supposed to get a tamarind leaf?

144
00:10:52,730 --> 00:10:53,700
Is this it?

145
00:10:56,630 --> 00:10:57,620
Or is it this one?

146
00:11:04,980 --> 00:11:05,935
It's probably this one.

147
00:11:18,950 --> 00:11:21,780
The sacred incantation to transform
tamarind leaves into hornets.

148
00:11:33,730 --> 00:11:37,780
Matyano Matya Matithisothaya

149
00:11:38,450 --> 00:11:39,740
Sapasa...

150
00:11:39,850 --> 00:11:41,860
Nomana thenasa

151
00:11:57,530 --> 00:12:02,300
Matyano Matya Matithisothaya Sapasa

152
00:12:03,170 --> 00:12:05,100
Nomana thenasa

153
00:12:17,065 --> 00:12:22,140
Matyano Matya Matithisothaya Sapasa

154
00:12:22,770 --> 00:12:23,580
Nomana

155
00:12:24,010 --> 00:12:25,060
thenasa

156
00:12:37,330 --> 00:12:38,580
What the hell is this uncle's stuff?

157
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:02,180
Hey, did you forget something?

158
00:13:13,170 --> 00:13:13,940
What the hell are you doing?!

159
00:13:15,370 --> 00:13:16,820
You dare betray the boss, huh?

160
00:13:18,010 --> 00:13:19,700
- Betray my ass!
- Hey!

161
00:13:28,970 --> 00:13:30,700
Ain't you a big mouth guy?

162
00:13:33,130 --> 00:13:34,540
You think you're tough, huh?

163
00:13:35,770 --> 00:13:38,220
Such a big mouth... let's kill him.

164
00:13:47,415 --> 00:13:48,660
You really eat a lot.

165
00:13:48,890 --> 00:13:49,860
Dessert too.

166
00:13:50,290 --> 00:13:51,100
So cute.

167
00:13:51,170 --> 00:13:53,620
She probably thinks this is her kitchen.

168
00:13:59,650 --> 00:14:00,340
Hey.

169
00:14:01,635 --> 00:14:03,010
Whoever wants to help her, you can.

170
00:14:03,595 --> 00:14:04,660
But me? I'm out.

171
00:14:05,970 --> 00:14:08,625
What kind of crazy girl is this?
She's tiny but eats like a monster.

172
00:14:09,365 --> 00:14:10,740
This isn't even called 'eating.'

173
00:14:11,510 --> 00:14:12,460
It's called 'stuffing'.

174
00:14:15,410 --> 00:14:17,580
Three plates by herself,
doesn't share with anyone.

175
00:14:18,290 --> 00:14:18,980
Look.

176
00:14:20,330 --> 00:14:22,340
Hear her chewing?

177
00:14:22,970 --> 00:14:25,060
Does she have any other symptoms?

178
00:14:26,290 --> 00:14:28,660
From what I can see,
she's healthier than us.

179
00:14:35,010 --> 00:14:35,780
Hey, you.

180
00:14:36,370 --> 00:14:37,700
You. Hey, you.

181
00:14:40,850 --> 00:14:43,060
Do you remember yet
who you are or where you're from?

182
00:14:51,245 --> 00:14:52,220
I don't remember.

183
00:14:53,680 --> 00:14:54,825
I just remember...

184
00:14:55,615 --> 00:14:56,620
being in the water.

185
00:14:57,670 --> 00:14:58,660
And then choking.

186
00:15:00,410 --> 00:15:01,020
And then...

187
00:15:02,475 --> 00:15:04,860
No matter how hard I think,
I can't remember.

188
00:15:06,770 --> 00:15:07,660
But it'll come back.

189
00:15:10,220 --> 00:15:11,100
She can talk.

190
00:15:11,700 --> 00:15:12,580
And she can eat.

191
00:15:13,340 --> 00:15:14,480
But she can't remember a damn thing.

192
00:15:18,395 --> 00:15:19,580
So what's your name?

193
00:15:21,730 --> 00:15:22,940
What is your name?

194
00:15:24,650 --> 00:15:25,420
I don't know.

195
00:15:28,250 --> 00:15:30,580
Should we give her a name first?
So we know what to call her.

196
00:15:32,370 --> 00:15:34,340
- Yeah, good idea.
- Yeah, let's name her.

197
00:15:39,170 --> 00:15:40,700
- How about 'Nam'? (Water)
- Huh?

198
00:15:41,735 --> 00:15:43,060
'Nam' is cute. Look at her.

199
00:15:44,250 --> 00:15:46,150
Man, you are so unimaginative.

200
00:15:46,290 --> 00:15:49,180
- You're no good at this.
- It's cute, look.

201
00:15:49,570 --> 00:15:53,100
But I think if 'Nam' stays with us,
it's good.

202
00:15:53,245 --> 00:15:56,180
She can help with work
to pay me back for the pizza.

203
00:15:56,690 --> 00:15:59,700
Look at this whole table.
I didn't get a single bite.

204
00:16:00,180 --> 00:16:02,460
Just the ghosts of shrimp
and the spirits of shellfish left.

205
00:16:02,670 --> 00:16:03,460
Want some?

206
00:16:03,620 --> 00:16:04,765
Ugh, go ahead and eat it, girl.

207
00:16:06,490 --> 00:16:08,020
Fine, let her stay for now.

208
00:16:09,370 --> 00:16:10,860
She's clever.
Her memory will probably come back.

209
00:16:14,970 --> 00:16:15,555
Nam.

210
00:16:16,650 --> 00:16:17,580
Nam.

211
00:16:18,945 --> 00:16:20,810
- Sister Nam.
- Hey, you.

212
00:16:21,850 --> 00:16:22,900
Your name is Nam.

213
00:16:23,330 --> 00:16:24,140
Do you understand?

214
00:16:25,330 --> 00:16:26,700
Your name is Nam.

215
00:16:57,175 --> 00:16:59,220
Some Russians came asking to buy pills.

216
00:17:00,410 --> 00:17:03,420
I told them we don't have any,
so they ordered from outside.

217
00:17:03,510 --> 00:17:04,700
Then some black guys came to deliver it.

218
00:17:06,690 --> 00:17:07,540
Do we have any at our shop?

219
00:17:08,450 --> 00:17:09,540
If you have it, you can tell me.

220
00:17:10,370 --> 00:17:12,260
I won't tell anyone.
I can even find buyers.

221
00:17:15,450 --> 00:17:16,220
I don't sell any.

222
00:17:17,650 --> 00:17:18,940
People are asking all the time.

223
00:17:20,050 --> 00:17:21,220
Don't you have any weed?

224
00:17:21,490 --> 00:17:22,260
I can help you sell.

225
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:29,215
Why does everyone think so poorly of me?

226
00:17:30,490 --> 00:17:34,180
I said I don't have it, that means I don't!
They never see me in a good light.

227
00:17:36,810 --> 00:17:38,780
When I'm poor,
people say I want to get rich.

228
00:17:40,130 --> 00:17:41,220
They already have it.

229
00:17:43,050 --> 00:17:44,180
It's us who still don't have it.

230
00:17:44,690 --> 00:17:47,610
When we try to make an honest living,
they accuse us of selling drugs.

231
00:17:48,950 --> 00:17:50,620
Or running scam gambling websites.

232
00:17:51,815 --> 00:17:53,300
Nothing good, ever.

233
00:17:54,855 --> 00:17:55,580
Why?

234
00:17:57,500 --> 00:17:59,220
Is it too hard to be a good person?

235
00:17:59,970 --> 00:18:00,580
Huh?

236
00:18:02,605 --> 00:18:04,020
Do we have to be wicked and evil?

237
00:18:05,460 --> 00:18:06,420
Hey.

238
00:18:07,055 --> 00:18:07,940
I'm sorry.

239
00:18:24,210 --> 00:18:27,180
(Murder at Toone's. Come quickly.)

240
00:18:33,010 --> 00:18:34,180
- Hello, uncle?
- Hello, Singh.

241
00:18:34,460 --> 00:18:36,060
Come to Toone's fast. There's trouble.

242
00:18:37,210 --> 00:18:38,140
Yeah, I'm coming right now.

243
00:18:44,170 --> 00:18:46,380
Shit, when are you getting here?

244
00:18:46,565 --> 00:18:47,980
- What happened, uncle?
- Singh.

245
00:18:48,395 --> 00:18:49,820
I saw them arguing loudly for a while.

246
00:18:50,145 --> 00:18:52,660
Didn't know who to call.
I think they have drugs inside.

247
00:18:52,775 --> 00:18:55,100
So I didn't dare call the cops.
It'll ruin the whole thing.

248
00:18:55,450 --> 00:18:58,260
But they've all left now.
I have nothing to do with this.

249
00:19:11,475 --> 00:19:12,140
Toone!

250
00:19:12,780 --> 00:19:13,530
Toone!

251
00:19:14,960 --> 00:19:16,220
What the hell happened?!

252
00:19:17,030 --> 00:19:17,900
Toone!

253
00:19:21,935 --> 00:19:23,220
It won't let go.

254
00:19:24,865 --> 00:19:27,180
Don't talk. I'll take you to the hospital.

255
00:19:27,855 --> 00:19:28,860
- Let's go.
- No.

256
00:19:31,735 --> 00:19:32,780
It's just...

257
00:19:44,370 --> 00:19:45,660
Hang in there, Toone.

258
00:19:46,955 --> 00:19:49,020
Who did this to you? Tell me.

259
00:19:49,290 --> 00:19:50,180
Tell me.

260
00:19:55,180 --> 00:19:57,300
You've done enough for me, Singh.

261
00:19:59,450 --> 00:20:01,300
Stop creating more karma.

262
00:20:15,090 --> 00:20:16,300
- Same as before.
- Mm-hmm.

263
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:17,660
Hey!

264
00:20:22,275 --> 00:20:22,940
Take it.

265
00:20:29,370 --> 00:20:32,420
What the hell? Why is it so little?
I ordered a lot more.

266
00:20:33,170 --> 00:20:34,460
Damn, you prick.

267
00:20:35,250 --> 00:20:36,580
This is all you get!

268
00:20:37,280 --> 00:20:38,105
What are you gonna do?

269
00:20:38,530 --> 00:20:39,580
You want it or not?

270
00:20:40,050 --> 00:20:43,020
You prick, if you don't want it,
get the hell out of my shop, okay?

271
00:20:43,290 --> 00:20:44,540
Get far away from me.

272
00:20:48,130 --> 00:20:49,100
Want it or not?

273
00:20:49,600 --> 00:20:51,260
Fine, I'll take it.

274
00:20:51,430 --> 00:20:53,140
Yeah, that's it. Done.

275
00:20:53,175 --> 00:20:54,420
- Take it. I'm a cop.
- Hey!

276
00:20:54,950 --> 00:20:57,140
- You bastard, you set me up?
- Yeah.

277
00:20:57,170 --> 00:20:57,940
Let go!

278
00:20:57,970 --> 00:21:00,820
Damn it, let go! Let go!

279
00:21:04,050 --> 00:21:05,140
Bro!

280
00:21:05,570 --> 00:21:06,860
- Bro!
- Weren't you a tough one?

281
00:21:07,130 --> 00:21:07,940
Singh!

282
00:21:08,290 --> 00:21:09,740
Hey, police!

283
00:21:12,050 --> 00:21:12,740
Singh!

284
00:21:14,610 --> 00:21:16,940
Shit, cops! Singh!

285
00:21:17,250 --> 00:21:18,140
Singh!

286
00:21:18,410 --> 00:21:20,060
Singh, go!

287
00:21:20,250 --> 00:21:21,405
You, come here!

288
00:21:23,450 --> 00:21:24,780
What the hell are you doing?!

289
00:21:29,965 --> 00:21:30,540
Toone!

290
00:21:31,265 --> 00:21:32,020
Toone!

291
00:21:34,040 --> 00:21:34,770
Toone!

292
00:21:36,770 --> 00:21:37,580
Toone!

293
00:21:38,490 --> 00:21:40,100
- Hey!
- Singh!

294
00:21:40,410 --> 00:21:41,220
Singh!

295
00:21:41,290 --> 00:21:42,340
Singh, go quickly!

296
00:21:42,370 --> 00:21:44,620
The cops will be here any minute,
you idiot! Get up, quick!

297
00:21:44,850 --> 00:21:47,500
Get up, Singh, go! Singh, get up!

298
00:21:47,690 --> 00:21:48,580
Singh!

299
00:21:48,650 --> 00:21:49,820
Go first, Singh!

300
00:21:50,115 --> 00:21:52,860
Damn it, hurry! Go! Go quickly!

301
00:22:11,225 --> 00:22:11,900
Fuck!

302
00:22:14,450 --> 00:22:17,420
I despise backstabbing dogs
like you the most.

303
00:22:19,130 --> 00:22:21,700
Do you know what I do to backstabbing dogs?

304
00:22:25,445 --> 00:22:30,700
How many times now have I been
betrayed by people I trusted?

305
00:22:34,380 --> 00:22:35,645
So many times.

306
00:22:36,165 --> 00:22:39,140
Again and again,
until I started losing faith.

307
00:22:40,770 --> 00:22:45,260
After that, I never trusted anyone again.
I never trusted anyone.

308
00:22:52,365 --> 00:22:54,220
It's starting to make me wonder.

309
00:22:54,810 --> 00:22:57,020
What do you really think of me?

310
00:22:59,315 --> 00:23:00,500
Am I just a plaything to you?

311
00:23:02,420 --> 00:23:05,300
You've never been afraid of me, have you?

312
00:23:07,730 --> 00:23:08,700
I am afraid.

313
00:23:09,770 --> 00:23:10,980
I am afraid of you!

314
00:23:11,990 --> 00:23:14,380
But I didn't do it! I really didn't do it!

315
00:23:14,810 --> 00:23:15,620
Anon.

316
00:23:21,010 --> 00:23:24,380
I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I did it! I did it!

317
00:23:28,580 --> 00:23:32,260
Because if I do anything you don't like,
you'll kill me, right?

318
00:23:34,570 --> 00:23:35,340
Ugh!

319
00:23:35,550 --> 00:23:39,420
I was scared you'd kill me,
so I had someone take care of you first.

320
00:23:40,105 --> 00:23:41,940
What would you have done? Huh?!

321
00:23:42,915 --> 00:23:45,220
I'm truly scared of you. I'm scared of you!

322
00:23:46,830 --> 00:23:49,275
What you're doing now...
that's not called 'being scared.'

323
00:23:51,465 --> 00:23:52,420
I'm really scared!

324
00:24:01,845 --> 00:24:03,220
I found the person you're looking for.

325
00:24:07,725 --> 00:24:10,180
The other night at the beach,
under the full moon.

326
00:24:12,615 --> 00:24:14,340
There was a group of kids.

327
00:24:15,090 --> 00:24:17,020
They helped someone out of the sea.

328
00:24:21,560 --> 00:24:24,900
So you're telling me this
to get me to forgive you?

329
00:24:25,370 --> 00:24:26,500
That's it, isn't it?

330
00:24:27,730 --> 00:24:32,100
No! I'm scared of you! I'm scared of you,
so I told you! Forgive...

331
00:24:33,160 --> 00:24:35,570
Please forgive me! Please forgive me!

332
00:24:35,650 --> 00:24:38,300
I just want you people to be honest.

333
00:24:38,690 --> 00:24:39,940
Is that so difficult?

334
00:24:51,820 --> 00:24:52,980
Pathetic.

335
00:24:57,905 --> 00:24:59,460
I know how to track them down.

336
00:25:01,150 --> 00:25:02,740
This isn't enough for you.

337
00:25:14,090 --> 00:25:15,220
I can give you everything.

338
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:17,940
These days...

339
00:25:18,930 --> 00:25:20,100
in this country...

340
00:25:21,450 --> 00:25:23,420
people don't respect
your spells and charms anymore.

341
00:25:24,250 --> 00:25:26,140
You need money. You need power.

342
00:25:27,670 --> 00:25:29,580
People respect these things nowadays.

343
00:25:30,870 --> 00:25:32,620
They don't respect your magic!

344
00:25:38,940 --> 00:25:40,025
I can get it for you.

345
00:25:42,025 --> 00:25:43,180
I can really get it for you.

346
00:26:26,620 --> 00:26:27,375
Sit with me.

347
00:26:46,500 --> 00:26:47,820
You look sad.

348
00:26:48,695 --> 00:26:49,580
Are you okay?

349
00:26:55,200 --> 00:26:56,100
I'm okay.

350
00:27:02,760 --> 00:27:03,820
It's so strange...

351
00:27:05,160 --> 00:27:07,020
Whenever I'm near you...

352
00:27:08,610 --> 00:27:09,500
I feel something strange.

353
00:27:11,380 --> 00:27:12,660
Have we met before?

354
00:27:15,640 --> 00:27:16,780
No.

355
00:27:25,400 --> 00:27:26,540
You know, people...

356
00:27:28,220 --> 00:27:32,220
Some people want to forget
everything from their past,

357
00:27:33,335 --> 00:27:34,300
but remember it all.

358
00:27:36,010 --> 00:27:37,380
But others...

359
00:27:38,770 --> 00:27:40,140
want to remember it all,

360
00:27:41,630 --> 00:27:43,020
but forget everything completely.

361
00:27:44,420 --> 00:27:45,660
It's so contradictory.

362
00:27:49,850 --> 00:27:50,860
What about you?

363
00:27:52,125 --> 00:27:53,220
Have you remembered anything yet?

364
00:27:55,610 --> 00:27:56,180
Heh.

365
00:27:56,530 --> 00:27:57,620
Not yet.

366
00:28:00,180 --> 00:28:02,900
I try and try, but I can't remember.

367
00:28:05,600 --> 00:28:08,260
I only see images under water...

368
00:28:09,015 --> 00:28:11,020
and then an image of all white,
filling my head.

369
00:28:14,115 --> 00:28:16,420
But I like this feeling.

370
00:28:17,230 --> 00:28:20,220
Not remembering means not
having to take responsibility for anything.

371
00:28:22,250 --> 00:28:24,780
Who knows, I might have been...

372
00:28:26,370 --> 00:28:27,540
a thief.

373
00:28:28,290 --> 00:28:30,820
Or a murderer.

374
00:28:31,635 --> 00:28:33,700
Or I might have done bad things to others.

375
00:28:36,170 --> 00:28:38,100
Not remembering is good. I like it.

376
00:28:50,950 --> 00:28:51,540
Hey!

377
00:28:53,255 --> 00:28:54,700
We have tattoos the same!

378
00:28:56,210 --> 00:28:57,460
Then we're the same kind of people.

379
00:28:58,890 --> 00:29:00,020
The kind with a past.

380
00:29:02,480 --> 00:29:04,100
But why did you get it tattooed?

381
00:29:06,570 --> 00:29:08,220
The tattooes protect me from bad things.

382
00:29:10,210 --> 00:29:11,500
So that means...

383
00:29:12,065 --> 00:29:14,180
you must have something bad
trying to enter your body,

384
00:29:14,530 --> 00:29:15,540
so you need to protect it?

385
00:29:19,770 --> 00:29:21,020
Yes, to protect it.

386
00:29:24,350 --> 00:29:25,940
Why block it?

387
00:29:26,730 --> 00:29:28,100
Who would just let them do it one-sidedly?

388
00:29:28,990 --> 00:29:29,980
Fight back!

389
00:30:37,740 --> 00:30:38,820
Doo!

390
00:31:38,735 --> 00:31:40,260
Rest in peace, brother.

391
00:31:49,490 --> 00:31:51,430
We should hurry and tell
the people at Ban Rajan.

392
00:31:51,830 --> 00:31:53,780
The Burmese know we're here.

393
00:31:54,890 --> 00:31:55,460
Mm-hmm.

394
00:31:57,730 --> 00:31:58,780
I think we should have Thong...

395
00:32:00,410 --> 00:32:01,540
go tell the Ban Rajan villagers.

396
00:32:02,530 --> 00:32:03,780
He knows the routes well.

397
00:32:21,730 --> 00:32:23,740
Just waiting for the blood, earth...

398
00:32:23,890 --> 00:32:27,405
water, wind, and fire to open this book.

399
00:32:34,175 --> 00:32:36,620
Then no one will be able to resist me.

400
00:32:44,190 --> 00:32:45,340
Earth.

401
00:32:47,350 --> 00:32:48,180
Water.

402
00:32:49,590 --> 00:32:50,420
Wind.

403
00:32:53,430 --> 00:32:54,420
Fire.

404
00:33:14,170 --> 00:33:17,660
Foon, today you take the staff meal money
out of the budget.

405
00:33:18,450 --> 00:33:20,060
Damn, we're over budget now!

406
00:33:20,850 --> 00:33:21,900
Son of a bitch.

407
00:33:24,570 --> 00:33:25,380
Delicious.

408
00:33:26,170 --> 00:33:28,060
Where'd one person go? Where's Toone?

409
00:33:29,820 --> 00:33:31,060
Toone said his mom came to visit.

410
00:33:31,090 --> 00:33:32,140
He'll be back this evening.

411
00:33:32,730 --> 00:33:33,780
Mom came to visit...

412
00:33:39,570 --> 00:33:40,180
Hey.

413
00:33:41,610 --> 00:33:42,460
Look at this.

414
00:33:43,010 --> 00:33:45,340
Man, I'm so damn sick of this.

415
00:33:45,490 --> 00:33:48,220
These people who steal from the country and
still hold their heads high.

416
00:33:48,330 --> 00:33:50,540
When the hell will they just be gone?

417
00:33:51,240 --> 00:33:52,810
Cheating and stuffing themselves.

418
00:33:52,885 --> 00:33:54,980
They can't take a damn
thing with them when they die.

419
00:33:55,410 --> 00:33:58,460
Look at him! How many times has he run,
and won every time?

420
00:33:59,050 --> 00:34:00,700
I don't even know who to blame anymore.

421
00:34:02,560 --> 00:34:04,700
- Have you ever voted?
- Never.

422
00:34:05,570 --> 00:34:07,780
- Damn it!
- Ugh!

423
00:34:08,730 --> 00:34:09,460
Hey!

424
00:34:10,410 --> 00:34:12,020
I have to go help my aunt
close the shop.

425
00:34:12,350 --> 00:34:13,195
Yeah, Singh.

426
00:34:13,730 --> 00:34:16,060
That clothes shop is having a sale.
Take Nam to look.

427
00:34:16,370 --> 00:34:17,620
Now she only wears my stuff.

428
00:34:17,970 --> 00:34:19,540
- Maybe she'll like something new.
- Which shop?

429
00:34:19,600 --> 00:34:21,265
The one behind you!

430
00:34:21,530 --> 00:34:24,260
Go check it. Maybe Nam wants a new outfit.

431
00:34:26,170 --> 00:34:26,980
Go on.

432
00:34:27,450 --> 00:34:28,980
Go, Jo, come help me. Go.

433
00:34:29,330 --> 00:34:30,540
- He hit me again!
- Yeah, you animal.

434
00:34:39,865 --> 00:34:41,020
What's up, kid?

435
00:34:41,715 --> 00:34:42,660
Any news?

436
00:34:46,585 --> 00:34:48,145
A woman with sacred tattoos...

437
00:34:48,635 --> 00:34:50,460
name unknown, emerged from the sea.

438
00:34:50,985 --> 00:34:52,980
Can't remember her name or anything.

439
00:34:53,350 --> 00:34:55,900
We're currently checking to see
who she is and where she's from.

440
00:34:56,715 --> 00:34:58,580
The tattoos are likely
from the same source.

441
00:34:59,290 --> 00:35:00,740
Sergeant, you should go check it out.

442
00:35:01,090 --> 00:35:02,620
What we know from Singh:

443
00:35:03,160 --> 00:35:05,260
He isn't directly involved
in the incident at Toone's bar.

444
00:35:05,390 --> 00:35:06,500
He was just present.

445
00:35:07,450 --> 00:35:09,740
But he's still linked to
the major drug shipment case.

446
00:35:10,130 --> 00:35:11,580
Though it's unclear...

447
00:35:12,330 --> 00:35:15,380
if these networks are still involved
with those gangs.

448
00:35:19,175 --> 00:35:21,885
We need to gather more evidence
to trace it back to them.

449
00:35:22,490 --> 00:35:25,060
I think their network is getting
bigger and bigger now.

450
00:35:25,570 --> 00:35:28,420
It's reaching local leaders
and politicians.

451
00:35:29,170 --> 00:35:31,335
We need to dig deeper.

452
00:35:31,490 --> 00:35:33,110
I believe this gang...

453
00:35:33,930 --> 00:35:35,870
It can definitely lead us to the source.

454
00:35:38,410 --> 00:35:39,950
Just be careful out there, Sergeant.

455
00:35:41,140 --> 00:35:41,980
I will.

456
00:35:47,090 --> 00:35:47,700
Hey.

457
00:35:52,650 --> 00:35:53,380
Is this one good?

458
00:35:53,890 --> 00:35:57,300
Because you're 'Singh' (Lion)
and this is a tiger. Lion and tiger.

459
00:36:00,370 --> 00:36:01,220
Tiger.

460
00:36:02,410 --> 00:36:03,060
You like it?

461
00:36:03,490 --> 00:36:05,380
Mm-hmm. Will you buy it for me?

462
00:36:08,065 --> 00:36:09,220
How many should I buy?

463
00:36:09,935 --> 00:36:11,060
How many do you want?

464
00:36:17,930 --> 00:36:18,700
Boss.

465
00:36:19,490 --> 00:36:22,740
We found someone who looks similar
to the person you're looking for.

466
00:36:23,010 --> 00:36:25,300
Around Walking Street. It's probably her.

467
00:36:29,015 --> 00:36:29,980
Let her go for now.

468
00:36:30,415 --> 00:36:31,860
Don't let her know yet.

469
00:36:35,065 --> 00:36:37,260
To catch a big fish,
you don't need big bait.

470
00:36:38,490 --> 00:36:39,655
Small bait is enough.

471
00:36:41,530 --> 00:36:42,660
It'll get caught on its own.

472
00:36:48,345 --> 00:36:48,860
Go.

473
00:36:54,090 --> 00:36:56,020
I'll take this cash
to the politicians first.

474
00:36:57,620 --> 00:36:59,260
Said I'd give it to them one last time.

475
00:37:02,020 --> 00:37:03,540
Talk about running the city together.

476
00:37:04,455 --> 00:37:06,580
But they take everything
that should be mine!

477
00:37:08,925 --> 00:37:09,900
Just watch.

478
00:37:10,455 --> 00:37:14,695
I won't let those old-timers
to cut me out like I'm worthless.

479
00:37:15,420 --> 00:37:17,740
I'll take back everything
that's rightfully mine.

480
00:37:22,800 --> 00:37:23,700
Seriously though...

481
00:37:24,965 --> 00:37:26,180
It'd be better if you took over instead.

482
00:37:31,835 --> 00:37:32,940
What's up?

483
00:37:33,615 --> 00:37:34,580
Want in?

484
00:37:43,770 --> 00:37:44,820
Sorry, Auntie.

485
00:37:45,330 --> 00:37:47,380
Our bar plays music for young people,
not Patsy Cline.

486
00:37:47,570 --> 00:37:50,050
Wow, Jo, your mouth...

487
00:37:50,450 --> 00:37:54,260
- Give him a scold! Teach him!
- It's good this bar still has customers.

488
00:37:54,370 --> 00:37:55,740
They like this style.

489
00:37:56,735 --> 00:37:57,620
Lots of people.

490
00:37:58,130 --> 00:38:00,060
Even with a DJ with a dog mouth.

491
00:38:00,530 --> 00:38:03,500
- A smelly dog mouth!
- I brushed my teeth, you bastard!

492
00:38:05,650 --> 00:38:08,380
- Oh! Mom, what are you doing here?
- Singh!

493
00:38:09,370 --> 00:38:11,900
I just wanted to see the bar.

494
00:38:12,370 --> 00:38:13,620
You never invite me.

495
00:38:14,955 --> 00:38:16,320
This is a bar, Mom.

496
00:38:16,610 --> 00:38:17,460
So what?

497
00:38:17,810 --> 00:38:19,820
- It's a bar, so I can't come?
- Hmm.

498
00:38:21,250 --> 00:38:22,180
Is this your girlfriend?

499
00:38:22,490 --> 00:38:23,285
Yes, Mom.

500
00:38:23,375 --> 00:38:25,540
- You'll see her when she's knocked up.
- Damn it, Jo!

501
00:38:26,170 --> 00:38:27,340
Don't listen to him, Mom.

502
00:38:28,600 --> 00:38:30,165
A friend named Nam.

503
00:38:30,835 --> 00:38:31,860
Hello, Auntie.

504
00:38:32,275 --> 00:38:33,220
Wow.

505
00:38:33,640 --> 00:38:35,700
This one is covered in tattoos, huh?

506
00:38:39,350 --> 00:38:41,940
Did you guys get into some kind of trouble?

507
00:38:44,915 --> 00:38:47,740
Is everything okay, Auntie?
You seemed stressed since yesterday.

508
00:38:49,530 --> 00:38:53,380
For several days now, there's been a car
circling the bar more and more often.

509
00:38:53,570 --> 00:38:56,580
Driving around so much it's clear
they're looking for someone.

510
00:38:58,640 --> 00:39:01,020
You boys haven't gotten into
any trouble, have you?

511
00:39:01,575 --> 00:39:03,340
If there's something, tell me.

512
00:39:03,480 --> 00:39:05,005
Don't think I don't know.

513
00:39:10,420 --> 00:39:12,060
Have you eaten, Mom? Are you hungry?

514
00:39:13,605 --> 00:39:14,460
Right here.

515
00:39:14,985 --> 00:39:17,620
Had a small beer. I'm about to head back.

516
00:39:18,000 --> 00:39:19,540
Just wanted to stop by and see.

517
00:39:23,610 --> 00:39:25,020
I bless your bar...

518
00:39:25,730 --> 00:39:28,535
May it prosper, thrive,
and be full of luck.

519
00:39:29,170 --> 00:39:30,905
- Amen.
- Amen.

520
00:39:30,955 --> 00:39:31,580
Thank you, Mom.

521
00:39:35,130 --> 00:39:38,340
Alright, Jo, come send me home.

522
00:39:38,610 --> 00:39:41,460
- Going home already?
- Not having another bottle, sis?

523
00:39:42,290 --> 00:39:44,260
What the hell are you asking
my mom to drink? Huh?!

524
00:39:44,325 --> 00:39:46,420
Ugh! The day you weren't
here, your mom drank a tower!

525
00:39:48,690 --> 00:39:51,420
Alright then, I'll take the keys
and drive your mother home.

526
00:39:52,130 --> 00:39:54,260
Drive carefully.
Don't crash with my mom.

527
00:39:54,290 --> 00:39:56,060
If your mom crashes, I crash too.

528
00:39:56,110 --> 00:39:57,470
Worry about me!
I've got a long future!

529
00:39:57,590 --> 00:39:58,380
Let's go, sis!

530
00:39:58,770 --> 00:40:00,820
Ouch! Oh...

531
00:40:00,915 --> 00:40:03,260
Singh, you bastard, your
mom is violent when drunk.

532
00:40:03,530 --> 00:40:04,700
- Bye, Auntie!
- Yeah.

533
00:40:04,810 --> 00:40:06,500
Hurry up, girl, I'm in a rush.

534
00:40:11,010 --> 00:40:12,580
When did my mom get here?

535
00:40:13,500 --> 00:40:14,540
A while ago.

536
00:40:15,090 --> 00:40:17,540
- Why?
- And you didn't even call me?

537
00:40:18,525 --> 00:40:20,300
Just letting her be chill.

538
00:40:34,610 --> 00:40:38,460
Hey, why are
donations so low this month?

539
00:40:38,930 --> 00:40:42,500
Oh brother, maybe the economy is bad.
They're probably waiting for the election.

540
00:40:50,330 --> 00:40:52,020
Was it you who killed Toone, you fuck?!

541
00:40:53,170 --> 00:40:53,740
Hey!

542
00:41:00,450 --> 00:41:02,140
You bastard, don't!

543
00:41:03,755 --> 00:41:05,340
Someone ordered me to do it.

544
00:41:06,010 --> 00:41:07,100
Please don't.

545
00:41:07,635 --> 00:41:11,820
Don't you get into any trouble.
If there's something, just tell me.

546
00:41:12,250 --> 00:41:13,580
Don't think I don't know.

547
00:41:16,050 --> 00:41:17,740
Have you eaten, Mom? Are you hungry?

548
00:41:18,210 --> 00:41:20,580
I'm going back. Just stopped by to see.

549
00:41:26,080 --> 00:41:27,660
I bless your bar...

550
00:41:27,850 --> 00:41:30,420
May it prosper, thrive, and full of luck.

551
00:41:31,010 --> 00:41:32,820
- Amen.
- Amen.

552
00:41:32,870 --> 00:41:33,460
Thank you, Mom.

553
00:41:37,075 --> 00:41:37,980
Don't.

554
00:42:30,650 --> 00:42:31,420
Hey! Hey!

555
00:42:31,450 --> 00:42:33,540
Nam! Hey, Nam!

556
00:42:34,105 --> 00:42:34,700
Nam!

557
00:42:35,850 --> 00:42:36,700
Are you okay?

558
00:42:41,350 --> 00:42:42,380
Nam, are you okay?

559
00:42:46,175 --> 00:42:48,780
You're not even fully recovered
and you got a contact high.

560
00:42:49,590 --> 00:42:50,785
Sit and rest a bit.

561
00:42:54,770 --> 00:42:55,660
Can I go...

562
00:42:56,095 --> 00:42:57,425
get some fresh air outside?

563
00:42:58,150 --> 00:42:58,940
I'm dizzy.

564
00:43:00,980 --> 00:43:01,980
But it's nice.

565
00:43:03,005 --> 00:43:04,820
Go over there. Go enjoy yourself outside.

566
00:43:05,565 --> 00:43:06,820
Call if you need anything.

567
00:43:07,595 --> 00:43:09,300
- Mm-hmm.
- Mm-hmm.

568
00:43:32,605 --> 00:43:34,300
You disappeared with the new shirt.

569
00:43:35,155 --> 00:43:36,660
Came back with a changed one.

570
00:43:37,695 --> 00:43:39,420
What have you been up to?

571
00:43:49,800 --> 00:43:53,020
You know, you can tell me anything.

572
00:43:54,330 --> 00:43:55,940
I think we're not that different morally.

573
00:44:06,670 --> 00:44:08,100
If you don't want to talk,
you don't have to.

574
00:44:08,815 --> 00:44:10,180
I don't really want to know.

575
00:44:19,525 --> 00:44:23,300
Hey, I just remembered
something about myself.

576
00:44:27,170 --> 00:44:27,980
What did you remember?

577
00:44:29,090 --> 00:44:30,100
I remember that...

578
00:44:31,290 --> 00:44:32,180
there was a boat.

579
00:44:33,890 --> 00:44:35,100
Full of money everywhere.

580
00:44:36,490 --> 00:44:39,660
And an old, ancient-looking book.

581
00:44:40,435 --> 00:44:41,700
It looked scary, too.

582
00:44:45,040 --> 00:44:46,020
An ancient book?

583
00:44:50,890 --> 00:44:51,860
And then...

584
00:44:53,485 --> 00:44:54,460
I can't remember anything else.

585
00:45:18,085 --> 00:45:18,740
Sir...

586
00:45:19,815 --> 00:45:22,460
Our boys who went to smash
Toone's place got shot to pieces.

587
00:45:25,110 --> 00:45:26,140
Mm-hmm.

588
00:45:47,410 --> 00:45:48,580
Hey, old friend.

589
00:45:52,680 --> 00:45:54,020
Let's go for a ride and talk.

590
00:46:05,825 --> 00:46:06,940
Haven't been here in a while.

591
00:46:07,770 --> 00:46:09,900
Huh, it's all renovated. Looks good.

592
00:46:14,620 --> 00:46:15,660
Why are you here?

593
00:46:15,985 --> 00:46:16,740
What do you want?

594
00:46:26,170 --> 00:46:27,260
Was it you?

595
00:46:28,590 --> 00:46:29,860
Who shot my guys last night?

596
00:46:32,665 --> 00:46:33,580
Hey.

597
00:46:35,090 --> 00:46:36,660
We quit everything.

598
00:46:37,660 --> 00:46:38,685
In the past...

599
00:46:39,460 --> 00:46:40,900
we did everything for you.

600
00:46:42,395 --> 00:46:44,020
What more do you want from us?

601
00:46:46,370 --> 00:46:47,910
About Toone, who died...

602
00:46:49,560 --> 00:46:52,255
- You gave the order, didn't you?
- I didn't order it.

603
00:46:55,040 --> 00:46:55,860
I did it myself.

604
00:47:48,535 --> 00:47:49,260
Boss.

605
00:47:49,415 --> 00:47:50,100
What's up.

606
00:47:55,850 --> 00:47:58,500
Didn't I tell you? You don't say no to me.

607
00:48:00,290 --> 00:48:02,420
You took my stuff on me
until you couldn't manage.

608
00:48:03,490 --> 00:48:05,900
And now you claim you've quit,
want to be a good person?

609
00:48:06,800 --> 00:48:08,675
I'm sorry, boss. I won't do it again, boss.

610
00:48:08,780 --> 00:48:09,820
I'm sorry, boss.

611
00:48:09,920 --> 00:48:13,180
- I'm sorry! I'm sorry, boss!
- You couldn't pay me back for what you took!

612
00:48:15,770 --> 00:48:17,940
Why do I have to deal
with people like you?

613
00:48:18,210 --> 00:48:19,020
Huh?

614
00:48:22,570 --> 00:48:23,940
I worked hard to earn a living.

615
00:48:24,370 --> 00:48:26,660
Kissing ass in the morning,
bowing in the evening.

616
00:48:27,770 --> 00:48:29,420
Being their servant.

617
00:48:29,960 --> 00:48:33,660
Just to become a big boss,
to feed scum like you.

618
00:48:41,565 --> 00:48:42,620
And that's still not enough?

619
00:48:44,045 --> 00:48:45,980
You even dared to become
a snitch for the cops.

620
00:48:47,800 --> 00:48:49,580
No, boss, I never did.

621
00:48:50,330 --> 00:48:51,500
I never did it, boss.

622
00:49:08,320 --> 00:49:09,180
And one more thing.

623
00:49:09,950 --> 00:49:11,460
I really don't like it.

624
00:49:13,710 --> 00:49:14,860
I don't like the look of you.

625
00:49:32,085 --> 00:49:33,060
Boss.

626
00:49:33,930 --> 00:49:37,220
It's not the police informant.
It's another person.

627
00:49:48,850 --> 00:49:49,660
You fuck!

628
00:49:58,260 --> 00:49:59,620
Not a smart move to do this.

629
00:50:02,130 --> 00:50:03,060
You guys...

630
00:50:04,160 --> 00:50:06,060
just love doing stupid things
over and over.

631
00:50:09,595 --> 00:50:10,580
Try to be smarter sometime.

632
00:50:12,875 --> 00:50:14,620
Even Toone, your friend,
didn't curse at me.

633
00:50:21,300 --> 00:50:22,500
Why did you kill Toone?

634
00:50:23,875 --> 00:50:25,780
I already did time for you!

635
00:50:26,950 --> 00:50:28,260
What more do you want from me?

636
00:50:29,105 --> 00:50:29,820
Huh?

637
00:50:30,415 --> 00:50:32,140
I asked why you killed him!

638
00:50:38,305 --> 00:50:39,500
Or do you want to go back inside?

639
00:50:41,885 --> 00:50:42,940
Go ahead.

640
00:50:44,625 --> 00:50:45,580
Shoot.

641
00:50:48,200 --> 00:50:49,900
The gunshot would probably
be heard downstairs.

642
00:50:53,600 --> 00:50:54,860
Your mom would probably hear it.

643
00:50:55,750 --> 00:50:57,580
Your friend Toone
would probably hear it from hell.

644
00:51:00,170 --> 00:51:00,940
You fuck!

645
00:51:07,410 --> 00:51:08,940
You really dare to shoot me?

646
00:51:12,385 --> 00:51:13,140
You fuck!

647
00:51:14,980 --> 00:51:16,740
The bullets ran out last night!

648
00:51:21,570 --> 00:51:22,620
Remember this.

649
00:51:23,315 --> 00:51:26,150
No one tells me what to do!
And don't meddle in my affairs.

650
00:51:30,510 --> 00:51:32,620
One day, I'll collect my karmic debt.

651
00:51:35,500 --> 00:51:37,780
If I order you to live, you live.

652
00:51:37,975 --> 00:51:39,980
If I order you to die, you die.

653
00:51:41,570 --> 00:51:43,660
You owe me for life, Singh.

654
00:51:44,690 --> 00:51:45,540
Remember that.

655
00:51:54,730 --> 00:51:56,020
You fucker!
